WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.322
[SEAGULLS CAWING]

2
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.580
JERICO: They messed with my brain.

3
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.620
Thought they knew what they'd get.

4
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.051
But they were wrong.

5
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.660
They don't know me.

6
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.860
I don't know what happens next,
but this I do know.

7
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.090
You hurt me, I hurt you worse.

8
00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.082
[♪♪♪]

9
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:15.205
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]
- [TRAFFIC NOISES]

10
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.286
Excuse me.

11
00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.780
Hi there. My wife was in last week

12
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.020
and she ordered a brown duffle in leather.

13
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.820
We were only able to locate in black, sir.

14
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.082
Well, she'll be very disappointed.

15
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.100
Right.

16
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.850
Okay, thank you very much.

17
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.280
[DOOR CLOSES]

18
00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.891
[PHONE RINGING]

19
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.780
- Hey, Jillie.
- No, Daddy, it's Emma.

20
00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.860
I can't find my Elly.

21
00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.140
Hey, baby, we'll find it. Put Mommy on.

22
00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.208
Mommy, it's Daddy.

23
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.008
- Hey, Billy.
- Hey, Jillie.

24
00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.820
When are you coming home?

25
00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.764
That depends really. What are you wearing?

26
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.340
Lingerie.

27
00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.340
Same thing I always wear
when I pick up Emma from school.

28
00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.283
That explains the good grades
she's been getting.

29
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.260
Hello? Billy?

30
00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.100
Um, listen, I gotta go. I'm gonna call
you back a little bit later.

31
00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.540
All right, baby. Love you.

32
00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.005
[TIRES SCREECHING]

33
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.240
[BEEPS]

34
00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.322
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

35
00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.929
[BEEPING]

36
00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.562
Hey! That's my bike!

37
00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.086
So we lost him off the bridge,

38
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.900
but he has three options
at the roundabout.

39
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.620
Waterloo Road, Stamford Street,
and Waterloo Bridge.

40
00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.802
He's been off the grid for 20 minutes.

41
00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.340
I want two by twos
out from the roundabout.

42
00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.761
- Hey, Charlie, re-wreck every screen.
- Sir.

43
00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.260
Found him. Bank two.

44
00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.620
Duffle's gone. Money's gone.

45
00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.449
- QUAKER: Time stamp?
- It's now.

46
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.165
Hey.

47
00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.380
- CAB DRIVER: Where to, mate?
- Just drive.

48
00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.562
Please, thank you. Not too fast.

49
00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.160
It's a black cab.

50
00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:41.980
License number S-I-5-2-J-G-N. I'm on him.

51
00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.940
I-5-2...

52
00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:45.690
J-G-N.

53
00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:51.100
Boyd,

54
00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.089
William.

55
00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.580
Can I borrow your mobile, mate?
20 quid extra.

56
00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:03.900
- Borrow me phone?
- Yeah.

57
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.810
20 quid? One call, yeah?

58
00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.660
[CELL PHONE VIBRATING]

59
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.580
It's Billy.

60
00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.100
They're all over him.

61
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.100
Get him to the cement factory
in Deptford. We used it before.

62
00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.362
Get a laundry team rolling, now.

63
00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:29.020
We're going to a cement factory.
Hornlink Way, Deptford docks.

64
00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.940
I put it in your GPS, so just follow that.

65
00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.485
All right.

66
00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.620
GPS VOICE:
Road to destination has been calculated.

67
00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:38.121
[KEYS CLACKING]

68
00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:43.884
HEIMDAHL: The docks at Deptford.

69
00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.140
Very romantic.

70
00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.288
[RESUMES TYPING]

71
00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.127
[GPS VOICE]
Turn left at the next roundabout.

72
00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.882
[TIRES SCREECHING]

73
00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.730
Move, move, move.

74
00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.202
AGENT: Outside cement factory, sir.

75
00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:27.726
[TIRES SCREECHING]

76
00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.140
- This isn't a cement factory.
- Eh?

77
00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.180
This isn't a cement factory!

78
00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:45.980
Hornlink Way, Deptford. I mean,
the GPS don't lie, mate.

79
00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.320
Turn around.

80
00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:49.766
[COCKING GUN]

81
00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.247
[GROANS]

82
00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.366
[GRUNTS]

83
00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:16.449
[BREATHING HARD]

84
00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.330
[GUN CLICKS]

85
00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.180
Fuck!

86
00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:42.566
[GRUNTS]

87
00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.002
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

88
00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:07.380
- Do we have him?
- AGENT: We got nothing, sir.

89
00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:08.720
Nobody here.

90
00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:12.540
Do a GPS on that phone number.

91
00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.210
- Find him now.
- [BEEPING]

92
00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.410
[PIGEONS COOING]

93
00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:32.580
If you've never been to a slaughterhouse,

94
00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.420
you have to go.

95
00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:39.321
To see what we do to those poor animals.

96
00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.403
- [ELECTRICITY CRACKLES]
- They use this...

97
00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.340
A picana.

98
00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:48.580
Nasty way to push them towards their doom.

99
00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.500
[ELECTRICITY BUZZES]

100
00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.420
- [ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]
- [GRUNTS]

101
00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:56.260
[GROANING]

102
00:08:56.360 --> 00:09:00.220
- [BUZZING STOPS]
- [BELLOWING]

103
00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.890
Now where is our friend?

104
00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:06.740
- Billy...
- [GRUNTING IN PAIN]

105
00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.446
I respect your silence.

106
00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.608
I really do.

107
00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:17.448
The problem is, I need the Dutchman.

108
00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.500
Last chance.

109
00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.140
Fuck you, psycho!

110
00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.340
[ELECTRICITY BUZZING]

111
00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.124
[GROANS]

112
00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:28.571
[BUZZING INTENSIFIES]

113
00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.488
AGENT: Left. Go, go, go, move.

114
00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.606
Going silent.

115
00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.980
AGENT 1: Point established.
Just arrived on site, sir.

116
00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.780
Check right. Check right.

117
00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:58.740
AGENT 2: North perimeter is clear.

118
00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:00.649
AGENT 1: Bravo, copy.

119
00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:05.880
Go. Go. Go.

120
00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:08.980
Go.

121
00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.620
- AGENT 2: Action required.
- AGENT 1: We need a medic.

122
00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:12.580
Confirmed: Agent Pope.

123
00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:14.728
Perimeter secure.

124
00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:20.420
Agent not responsive.
Repeat, agent not responsive.

125
00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.204
Respiration negative.

126
00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:27.400
Ready for defib.

127
00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.204
- Charging paddles.
- AGENT 3: Clear.

128
00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:34.120
Clear!

129
00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:36.900
He's dead, sir.

130
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.286
Fuck!

131
00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.203
[♪♪♪]

132
00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.364
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

133
00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:57.642
Doctor, I'm so sorry, but this man says
he's with the government.

134
00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:04.100
Dr. Franks, I have one job at the moment,

135
00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:09.220
which is to get you onto a A400 airbus
sitting on a tarmac at Dover ASAP.

136
00:11:09.320 --> 00:11:11.660
Your memory program is going live.

137
00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.570
We have an officer down
and we need what only he knew.

138
00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:16.420
You're going to retrieve it for us.

139
00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.420
Does he have any brain activity?

140
00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:19.760
[FOLDER RUSTLES]

141
00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.963
That was taken a few hours ago.

142
00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.860
I am five years away from human trials.

143
00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:30.260
You have 48 hours to make this work.

144
00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:33.569
National security threat, highest level.

145
00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:36.220
Can you or can you not transfer memories

146
00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:38.220
from a dead mammal to a live one?

147
00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:39.560
Yeah.

148
00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:41.100
What do you need?

149
00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.820
I'll need my equipment,
I'll need my staff,

150
00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.740
I'll need a suitable, uh, recipient.

151
00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:47.260
D'you have any candidates?

152
00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:50.921
Um, they're not gonna like him.

153
00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:54.931
[DOOR BUZZING]

154
00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.721
WARDEN: Just so wherever
you're taking him knows...

155
00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:05.220
Jerico Stewart. He's in and out
of prison more than half his life.

156
00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.060
He's got no impulse control,
no sense of proportion.

157
00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:09.780
He's unable to calculate

158
00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:12.460
the potential negative
consequences of his actions.

159
00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.460
He has a total lack of empathy
for anybody or anything.

160
00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:16.846
[DOOR BUZZES]

161
00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:20.121
- Through.
- [DOOR BUZZES]

162
00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:27.260
He feels nothing. No hatred, no love.

163
00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:29.260
It gets worse.

164
00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:34.571
This is what was left of a gang member
who tried to recruit him.

165
00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.243
Truth is, I have no way to discipline him.

166
00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:43.649
You can't punish someone who doesn't
know they did anything wrong.

167
00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:46.180
He does not understand society

168
00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.700
or how people are supposed to behave.

169
00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.086
[DOOR BUZZES]

170
00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.660
Come on.

171
00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.683
- WARDEN: Hey, Jerico.
- Come on.

172
00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.882
These men are here to see you.

173
00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:09.370
They're taking you out.

174
00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:16.060
I haven't had my lunch.

175
00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.380
WARDEN: That's right.
Get Jerico his lunch.

176
00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.820
- JERICO: Yeah.
- Send in the lunch.

177
00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:23.811
That's right, get Jerico his lunch.

178
00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:26.500
GUARD OVER INTERCOM: Lunch in the hole.

179
00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:29.604
Come on. Yeah.

180
00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.324
- Yeah.
- [GRATE CLOSES]

181
00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:37.609
All right, enough of this shit.
Lunch is over.

182
00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:41.980
You're coming with us now. Let's go.

183
00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.320
I can't.

184
00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.380
I got a chain around my neck.

185
00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.404
[GRUNTS] Oh!

186
00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:55.328
You know you're gonna have
to use two of those.

187
00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:57.886
Oh!

188
00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:00.680
[JERICO GRUNTING]

189
00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:03.380
Yeah!

190
00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.289
[GROANING]

191
00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:09.740
You fuckers.

192
00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:13.731
Oh, you fuckers.

193
00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.080
Got him.

194
00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:19.420
WARDEN: That's it. Open the cell.

195
00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:20.885
- [DOOR BUZZES]
- Go!

196
00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:31.340
OPERATOR: Chopper Gamma EMHG special,

197
00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:34.540
you are clear for approach
on runway 2-2-Lima.

198
00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:36.608
You better wake him up.

199
00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:46.322
[RADIO CHATTER INDISTINCT]

200
00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.162
Give this to the doctor.

201
00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:34.960
[BEEPING]

202
00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.008
[JERICO CHUCKLES]

203
00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:47.971
DR. FRANKS: Any allergies, Jerico?

204
00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:52.060
- What?
- Anything you're allergic to?

205
00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:53.380
- Yeah, luck.
- Ha!

206
00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:56.220
Good kind or the bad kind?

207
00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:58.260
You tell me.

208
00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:00.260
We're all set, doctor.

209
00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.500
Any previous surgeries?

210
00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.125
Previous?

211
00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.849
I don't need no surgery... [GRUNTS]

212
00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:10.580
All right, hit him with 150 mg
of hydroxyzine.

213
00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:11.980
- That's enough of this.
- 150. Yes, sir.

214
00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:14.845
- [MONITOR BEEPING RAPIDLY]
- What are you doing to me?

215
00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:18.969
[GRUNTS] Ooh.

216
00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.687
- [MONITOR BEEPING STEADILY]
- Ooh...

217
00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.003
You had an injury to your head.

218
00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:30.420
You got hurt, right? When you were young.

219
00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:32.124
You remember how it happened?

220
00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:36.780
Yeah. My mother...

221
00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:39.980
told my Daddy that he wasn't my daddy.

222
00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:44.608
So he called her a whore
and threw me out the car window.

223
00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:49.048
I'm gonna take care of you, Jerico.

224
00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:53.340
[PIERS MORGAN]
My next guest is Xavier Heimdahl.

225
00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:56.740
He's best known as the founder
of Stone Harp Industries,

226
00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:59.900
makers of phone, computer
and communication systems.

227
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.260
Most recently, he was charged
with treason by the Spanish government.

228
00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:07.500
Mr. Heimdahl, how would you respond
to these very serious allegations?

229
00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:12.860
Well, if it's treasonous to call out
massive corruption at the highest levels

230
00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:15.940
and to expose political murders...

231
00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.820
Yes, then I'm guilty.

232
00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:22.020
But your accusations were never actually
proven in a court of law.

233
00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:25.727
Of course not. How could they be?

234
00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:29.246
The police, the judges and the courts

235
00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:33.060
are all part of the world's
most powerful criminal enterprise.

236
00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:37.260
So to clarify, you're calling for the
overthrow of the Spanish government.

237
00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:40.820
No, no, no. I'm calling for
the overthrow of all governments.

238
00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:42.922
Politicians, religious fanatics.

239
00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.060
Brainwashing by corporations,

240
00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:49.210
the corruption of the banking system...
Gone. Gone.

241
00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:53.900
Washington, Berlin, Beijing
will be graveyards.

242
00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:56.020
And only then people will understand

243
00:17:56.120 --> 00:17:58.180
there is a better way to run this world.

244
00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:01.620
And that's what you really want here,
worldwide revolution.

245
00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:05.100
Governments must fall.

246
00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.180
Got one.

247
00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.980
Elsa Mueller.
Former German Special Forces.

248
00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:11.340
One of Heimdahl's.

249
00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:14.842
Guys, you gotta roll.
Jerico Stewart is now landing.

250
00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:20.046
MARTA: Is Billy still breathing?

251
00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:21.740
HIGGS: Artificially breathing.

252
00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.220
The machine's keeping his body
alive but he's gone.

253
00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.180
- You see those diodes?
- MARTA: Mm.

254
00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:29.460
They deliver a micro charge
to his frontal lobe.

255
00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.460
Even though his brain is clinically dead,

256
00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.860
the charge fired the neurons one last time

257
00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:35.940
and lets us build a map
of the neuronal pattern.

258
00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:38.540
And then you transfer it
to the other guy's head?

