- Get your hands off him!

777
01:01:22.680 --> 01:01:24.091
[CHOKING]

778
01:01:24.200 --> 01:01:25.500
Stand down!

779
01:01:25.600 --> 01:01:26.840
[GRUNTS]

780
01:01:27.840 --> 01:01:29.922
[STRAINING]
Only you can put out this fire.

781
01:01:30.040 --> 01:01:32.140
The Dutchman.

782
01:01:32.240 --> 01:01:36.100
Where is he? And the money's yours.

783
01:01:36.200 --> 01:01:38.180
The money's mine?

784
01:01:38.280 --> 01:01:40.020
All of it.

785
01:01:40.120 --> 01:01:41.690
I want to go there.

786
01:01:41.800 --> 01:01:44.644
And the picture. Yeah.

787
01:01:44.760 --> 01:01:46.091
[EXHALES]

788
01:02:04.240 --> 01:02:06.811
Which way, Jerico?

789
01:02:16.800 --> 01:02:19.406
Right.

790
01:02:40.800 --> 01:02:42.040
[WHIRRING]

791
01:02:43.400 --> 01:02:44.640
[BEEPING]

792
01:02:49.000 --> 01:02:52.380
Sir, the facial recognition system
just picked up a red notice.

793
01:02:52.480 --> 01:02:55.006
QUAKER: Pull over! Pull over!

794
01:03:02.400 --> 01:03:04.820
Put the convict on ice and send him home.

795
01:03:04.920 --> 01:03:06.540
- That's it?
- The Dutchman's been flagged

796
01:03:06.640 --> 01:03:07.980
at London City airport.

797
01:03:08.080 --> 01:03:09.940
MI-5 are covering him.

798
01:03:10.040 --> 01:03:11.900
We're heading over.

799
01:03:12.000 --> 01:03:13.380
JERICO: Hey! Hey!

800
01:03:13.480 --> 01:03:14.900
Hey, my money.

801
01:03:15.000 --> 01:03:17.571
Hey! What about my money?

802
01:03:29.280 --> 01:03:31.282
[KEYS CLACKING]

803
01:04:14.480 --> 01:04:15.720
[COMPUTER WHIRRING]

804
01:04:15.840 --> 01:04:17.842
[ALARM BLARING]

805
01:04:20.720 --> 01:04:22.620
Elsa, he's yours now.

806
01:04:22.720 --> 01:04:24.882
I need him alive.

807
01:04:27.160 --> 01:04:28.571
I'm afraid it's not your man.

808
01:04:30.080 --> 01:04:31.764
[PANTS]

809
01:04:31.880 --> 01:04:33.484
[ENGINE REVVING]

810
01:04:46.520 --> 01:04:49.940
[GASPING] I'm hit!

811
01:04:50.040 --> 01:04:51.451
Give me the gun!

812
01:05:02.800 --> 01:05:04.086
Don't shoot him!

813
01:05:09.320 --> 01:05:10.651
[MAN GRUNTS]

814
01:05:13.760 --> 01:05:15.683
[TIRES SCREECHING]

815
01:05:58.040 --> 01:05:59.451
[MUFFLED SCREAMING]

816
01:06:11.440 --> 01:06:13.522
[SIRENS WAILING IN DISTANCE]

817
01:06:15.960 --> 01:06:19.442
Sir, we ordered a dive team
to search for Jerico's body.

818
01:06:20.440 --> 01:06:22.807
What a fucking mess.

819
01:06:24.000 --> 01:06:27.380
The Russians cannot be
allowed to make the buy.

820
01:06:27.480 --> 01:06:28.811
Blanket their embassy.

821
01:06:28.920 --> 01:06:30.940
Anything in, anything out gets covered.

822
01:06:31.040 --> 01:06:32.340
- Clear?
- Yes, sir.

823
01:06:32.440 --> 01:06:35.887
And that fucker Heimdahl's been
up our asses from the start.

824
01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:39.891
I want new passcodes, new firewalls.

825
01:06:40.000 --> 01:06:43.368
- Switch to military channels, got it?
- Yes, sir.

826
01:06:45.160 --> 01:06:47.162
[BELL TOLLING]

827
01:06:50.080 --> 01:06:53.540
REPORTER ON TV: Gunfire broke out
earlier today on the Connaught Bridge,

828
01:06:53.640 --> 01:06:58.460
with five confirmed fatalities
and numerous seriously injured.

829
01:06:58.560 --> 01:07:02.485
Authorities continue to search
for missing bodies in the river Thames.

830
01:07:04.240 --> 01:07:07.460
I'm really sorry that I lost him.
Maybe if I...

831
01:07:07.560 --> 01:07:09.927
If, if, if, if!

832
01:07:10.040 --> 01:07:13.300
If you had kept closer tabs
on the Dutchman,

833
01:07:13.400 --> 01:07:15.641
maybe we'd already have the Wormhole!

834
01:07:19.400 --> 01:07:22.882
I must say I'm not that happy
at the moment, Elsa.

835
01:07:24.240 --> 01:07:26.242
- Do you want me to leave?
- No.

836
01:07:31.840 --> 01:07:34.500
I apologize.

837
01:07:34.600 --> 01:07:36.204
Good.

838
01:07:40.840 --> 01:07:42.126
[ELSA SIGHS]

839
01:07:45.080 --> 01:07:47.811
HEIMDAHL: We need to find Jerico.

840
01:07:49.800 --> 01:07:51.802
[GROANS SOFTLY]

841
01:07:56.520 --> 01:07:58.284
[GRUNTS]

842
01:08:00.800 --> 01:08:03.406
[BEEPING]

843
01:08:12.240 --> 01:08:13.605
[GRUNTS]

844
01:08:20.680 --> 01:08:22.682
[MOANS]

845
01:08:27.760 --> 01:08:29.460
[GRUNTS]

846
01:08:29.560 --> 01:08:32.131
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

847
01:08:32.680 --> 01:08:33.966
[ALARM SYSTEM BEEPS]

848
01:08:39.000 --> 01:08:40.460
Mommy, can I watch TV?

849
01:08:40.560 --> 01:08:43.131
Sure, baby. Of course.

850
01:08:46.120 --> 01:08:47.724
[THUMPING IN DISTANCE]

851
01:08:52.120 --> 01:08:54.646
[CHILDREN'S MUSIC PLAYING ON TV]

852
01:09:17.880 --> 01:09:19.530
[COCKS GUN]

853
01:09:40.840 --> 01:09:42.780
What are you doing in my basement?

854
01:09:42.880 --> 01:09:45.087
[JERICO GRUNTS]

855
01:09:45.200 --> 01:09:46.531
What is all this?

856
01:09:47.880 --> 01:09:49.140
[CLATTERS]

857
01:09:49.240 --> 01:09:50.571
That belongs to Emma.

858
01:09:53.960 --> 01:09:55.740
Did you work with Billy?

859
01:09:55.840 --> 01:09:59.660
I don't think anyone like him

860
01:09:59.760 --> 01:10:03.140
ever would've worked
with somebody like me.

861
01:10:03.240 --> 01:10:06.403
They stuck Billy in my head.

862
01:10:07.560 --> 01:10:10.450
I got a scar. See?

863
01:10:10.560 --> 01:10:14.087
All the stuff that he knew,
all the stuff that he could do,

864
01:10:14.200 --> 01:10:15.929
I got it all scrambled up inside me.

865
01:10:18.040 --> 01:10:19.690
That's impossible.

866
01:10:21.240 --> 01:10:25.820
First car you two ever bought,
used... used Rover.

867
01:10:25.920 --> 01:10:27.420
It smelled like fish and chips.

868
01:10:27.520 --> 01:10:29.420
Bum clutch blew the first week.

869
01:10:29.520 --> 01:10:31.500
[GRUNTS]

870
01:10:31.600 --> 01:10:34.820
Cost you 1,100 quid to get it fixed.

871
01:10:34.920 --> 01:10:38.500
I told you. They stuck his brain in me.

872
01:10:38.600 --> 01:10:40.500
- That's enough.
- Mom?

873
01:10:40.600 --> 01:10:42.780
Mom, where are you? I'm hungry.

874
01:10:42.880 --> 01:10:44.882
Just a second, baby.

875
01:10:47.680 --> 01:10:51.241
Sunday night. Chicken and waffles.

876
01:10:52.880 --> 01:10:55.780
You do the chicken, I do the waffles.

877
01:10:55.880 --> 01:10:59.441
I know that she likes
the syrup on the bottom only.

878
01:11:00.440 --> 01:11:03.780
I get pieces.

879
01:11:03.880 --> 01:11:06.780
Things pop up.

880
01:11:06.880 --> 01:11:11.940
Different places, I... I see things.

881
01:11:12.040 --> 01:11:14.088
Don't ask me how they did it, but they...

882
01:11:15.160 --> 01:11:17.300
they did it.

883
01:11:17.400 --> 01:11:19.801
Why?

884
01:11:19.920 --> 01:11:21.160
Oh, God.

885
01:11:21.280 --> 01:11:24.500
They're looking for details about where
your husband stashed a guy

886
01:11:24.600 --> 01:11:25.886
before he was killed.

887
01:11:30.480 --> 01:11:34.883
Now, go feed your kid.
I'll finish here and...

888
01:11:42.640 --> 01:11:45.500
I'll finish here and get out.

889
01:11:45.600 --> 01:11:47.260
Leave you alone.

890
01:11:47.360 --> 01:11:48.600
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

891
01:11:50.680 --> 01:11:52.842
[JERICO SNIFFS AND GROANS]

892
01:11:56.320 --> 01:11:57.526
No.

893
01:12:00.800 --> 01:12:03.371
Billy could never hurt you, Jill,
so neither can I.

894
01:12:26.920 --> 01:12:28.365
[DOOR CLOSES]

895
01:12:41.360 --> 01:12:42.725
[SQUEALING]

896
01:12:48.720 --> 01:12:50.802
[GRUNTS]

897
01:13:01.360 --> 01:13:02.600
[CLOCK TICKING]

898
01:13:17.520 --> 01:13:20.091
[INDISTINCT SHOUTING]

899
01:13:21.480 --> 01:13:24.051
[COMPUTER BEEPING]

900
01:13:37.280 --> 01:13:39.540
[MONITOR BEEPING]

901
01:13:39.640 --> 01:13:42.460
Hot bird in tube 4, sir.

902
01:13:42.560 --> 01:13:44.100
- That's not possible.
- Guidance system's a go!

903
01:13:44.200 --> 01:13:46.441
- Tracking system's a go!
- Shut it down!

904
01:13:48.640 --> 01:13:49.971
I can't! We're locked out, sir!

905
01:13:57.680 --> 01:13:59.967
Missile away! Repeat! Missile away!

906
01:14:05.480 --> 01:14:08.980
Punch in the self-destruct code
before the fish can arm itself!

907
01:14:09.080 --> 01:14:11.890
Alpha 30, echo 40, Bravo Hotel.

908
01:14:13.480 --> 01:14:15.448
Negative. It's not responding.

909
01:14:31.040 --> 01:14:33.460
We're good. No nuke flash. We're good.

910
01:14:33.560 --> 01:14:35.289
[EXHALES]

911
01:14:36.960 --> 01:14:38.420
Jesus fucking Christ.

912
01:14:38.520 --> 01:14:40.220
SEAMAN:
We didn't terminate that missile, sir.

913
01:14:40.320 --> 01:14:42.846
[♪♪♪]

914
01:14:54.480 --> 01:14:56.084
[PANTING]

915
01:14:58.680 --> 01:15:01.490
Did you know I lost my Daddy?

916
01:15:03.280 --> 01:15:05.540
Yeah.

917
01:15:05.640 --> 01:15:08.928
He gave me Elly. For my birthday.

918
01:15:11.360 --> 01:15:14.260
If we don't go deeper,
his trunk's gonna stick out.

919
01:15:14.360 --> 01:15:16.442
- Go deeper.
- [SPADE CLANKING]

920
01:15:20.360 --> 01:15:22.260
Did you hurt yourself?

921
01:15:22.360 --> 01:15:23.600
[OVEN TIMER DINGS]

922
01:15:28.000 --> 01:15:29.240
[PLATE CLATTERS]

923
01:15:31.960 --> 01:15:34.020
Stop.

924
01:15:34.120 --> 01:15:35.420
Emma, come here, please.

925
01:15:35.520 --> 01:15:37.460
No, Mommy. We're burying my Elly.

926
01:15:37.560 --> 01:15:39.244
Come here.

927
01:15:40.360 --> 01:15:42.886
He said he was a friend of Daddy's.

928
01:15:44.080 --> 01:15:46.686
Leave. Please.

929
01:15:47.320 --> 01:15:50.210
Can he stay for dinner? He's nice.

930
01:15:51.200 --> 01:15:52.565
Emma, go inside.

931
01:15:56.720 --> 01:15:58.722
[MUTTERING]

932
01:16:01.600 --> 01:16:03.602
I'll do the waffles, then I'll go.

933
01:16:11.680 --> 01:16:13.489
[PLAYING MELODY]

934
01:16:22.840 --> 01:16:25.491
- Come and play.
- What?

935
01:16:25.600 --> 01:16:26.965
Come and play.

936
01:16:29.880 --> 01:16:31.540
I don't know how.

937
01:16:31.640 --> 01:16:32.880
I'll teach you.

938
01:16:37.600 --> 01:16:39.060
I don't know if this is such a good idea.

939
01:16:39.160 --> 01:16:41.401
It's fine. Come on.

940
01:16:43.880 --> 01:16:46.531
- Mm-hmm.
- Come on.

941
01:16:52.760 --> 01:16:55.860
So you just put your hands like this.

942
01:16:55.960 --> 01:16:58.340
Put your hand there.

943
01:16:58.440 --> 01:16:59.680
And then you go...

944
01:17:04.960 --> 01:17:06.420
[PLAYING PIANO]

945
01:17:06.520 --> 01:17:07.806
It's okay.

946
01:17:21.280 --> 01:17:23.260
That's right. And then you go again.

947
01:17:23.360 --> 01:17:24.646
[PIANO CONTINUES]

948
01:17:27.720 --> 01:17:30.620
Okay, Emma. It's late.

949
01:17:30.720 --> 01:17:32.140
It's time to go to bed.

950
01:17:32.240 --> 01:17:35.449
Yes, Mommy. Good night, Jerico.

951
01:17:37.520 --> 01:17:39.329
- Good night, Mommy.
- Good night, baby.

952
01:17:41.960 --> 01:17:43.644
[GRUNTS]

953
01:17:52.560 --> 01:17:53.891
Who are you?

954
01:17:58.680 --> 01:17:59.886
I don't know.

955
01:18:02.120 --> 01:18:03.884
Most of my life, a number.

956
01:18:06.360 --> 01:18:08.886
My brain don't always work right.

957
01:18:10.080 --> 01:18:13.700
I haven't always acted right.

958
01:18:13.800 --> 01:18:16.087
Having your man in my head made me...

959
01:18:18.200 --> 01:18:20.680
made me feel things. Know things.

960
01:18:22.280 --> 01:18:24.362
Right. Wrong.

961
01:18:26.320 --> 01:18:27.560
I guess it don't matter.

962
01:18:27.720 --> 01:18:30.803
Doc says it's all going away pretty soon.

963
01:18:32.480 --> 01:18:35.324
Can you feel what Billy felt?

964
01:18:38.200 --> 01:18:39.804
Can you?

965
01:18:44.160 --> 01:18:47.004
There was this funny thing
Billy used to do.

966
01:18:50.360 --> 01:18:52.886
[SOBS] This is too much.

967
01:18:58.360 --> 01:19:02.046
That was our signal that he loves me.

968
01:19:03.280 --> 01:19:05.647
I, uh...

969
01:19:05.760 --> 01:19:09.820
[GRUNTS] I know... I know...

970
01:19:09.920 --> 01:19:15.540
I know what that "love" word's
supposed to mean, but I...

971
01:19:15.640 --> 01:19:17.060
I never...

972
01:19:17.160 --> 01:19:18.650
Our wedding day.

973
01:19:19.640 --> 01:19:21.051
Do you remember?

974
01:19:22.480 --> 01:19:23.970
Yes.

975
01:19:25.600 --> 01:19:27.020
The beach.

976
01:19:27.120 --> 01:19:30.260
- First time I handed you Emma?
- Yeah...

977
01:19:30.360 --> 01:19:32.740
You were so happy.

978
01:19:32.840 --> 01:19:36.561
Yeah. I have... [SNIFFLES]

979
01:19:37.760 --> 01:19:40.180
I feel it.

980
01:19:40.280 --> 01:19:43.568
- I feel it. Yeah, I...
- [SNIFFLES]

981
01:19:47.800 --> 01:19:51.885
He loves you... so much.

982
01:19:59.960 --> 01:20:01.803
Where will you go now?

983
01:20:04.560 --> 01:20:08.804
I don't know, wherever he...
wherever he takes me.

984
01:20:10.440 --> 01:20:13.011
Then stay here.

985
01:20:13.120 --> 01:20:15.646
You can stay on the couch.

986
01:20:21.840 --> 01:20:24.411
It won't be the first time on that couch.

987
01:20:31.840 --> 01:20:33.780
TV REPORTER: Our top story,
a mystery missile

988
01:20:33.880 --> 01:20:36.100
that was launched
off the coast of Portugal.

989
01:20:36.200 --> 01:20:38.860
The question is,
where'd this missile come from?

990
01:20:38.960 --> 01:20:41.180
OBAMA ON TV: Our adversaries
are getting more sophisticated.

991
01:20:41.280 --> 01:20:43.282
[NEWS PLAYING ON TV]

992
01:20:46.440 --> 01:20:49.660
Good morning. Got you some fresh coffee.

993
01:20:49.760 --> 01:20:51.250
Thanks.

994
01:20:56.880 --> 01:20:59.850
Don't worry about it. It's okay.

995
01:21:01.640 --> 01:21:02.980
...where this missile came from,

996
01:21:03.080 --> 01:21:05.220
we won't know who will be held
accountable.

997
01:21:05.320 --> 01:21:09.609
This is now the smoking gun.
We have radar analysis...

998
01:21:16.960 --> 01:21:18.769
You work at the university.

999
01:21:18.880 --> 01:21:21.020
There's a cage in the library, right?

1000
01:21:21.120 --> 01:21:22.700
A bookcase with a key.

1001
01:21:22.800 --> 01:21:24.580
Yeah, the rare book collection.

1002
01:21:24.680 --> 01:21:26.420
Billy and I used to go there sometimes.

1003
01:21:26.520 --> 01:21:28.060
- Why? Does this have something...?
- Yes.

1004
01:21:28.160 --> 01:21:29.446
Yes.

1005
01:21:30.760 --> 01:21:32.340
Everything.

1006
01:21:32.440 --> 01:21:33.780
I'll need a car.

1007
01:21:33.880 --> 01:21:35.900
And the key for the books.

1008
01:21:36.000 --> 01:21:38.480
- Sure. Yeah.
- [KEYS JANGLING]

1009
01:21:42.800 --> 01:21:44.380
We're gonna have money, Jill.

1010
01:21:44.480 --> 01:21:46.084
Lots of it.

1011
01:21:55.200 --> 01:21:56.964
I wish I could keep being him.

1012
01:22:20.240 --> 01:22:22.500
Emma? Come upstairs, please!

1013
01:22:22.600 --> 01:22:23.931
Coming!

1014
01:22:25.200 --> 01:22:27.660
Come. We need to take a shower.

1015
01:22:27.760 --> 01:22:29.967
- Did you lock the door downstairs?
- Yeah.

1016
01:22:39.120 --> 01:22:40.360
[GASPS]

1017
01:22:43.960 --> 01:22:45.849
Where is Jerico?

1018
01:22:55.120 --> 01:22:56.690
[GRUNTING]

1019
01:23:11.160 --> 01:23:12.400
[GRUNTS]

1020
01:23:37.240 --> 01:23:40.926
Yeah. Georgie Orwell.

1021
01:23:47.960 --> 01:23:49.200
[GRUNTS]

1022
01:23:51.200 --> 01:23:52.804
Yeah.

1023
01:24:01.040 --> 01:24:02.280
[GRUNTS]

1024
01:24:07.920 --> 01:24:09.365
Oh.

1025
01:24:11.200 --> 01:24:12.929
You're the guy who killed me.

1026
01:24:13.040 --> 01:24:15.300
Good memory.

1027
01:24:15.400 --> 01:24:17.050
Yeah.

1028
01:24:21.040 --> 01:24:24.123
You hurt me. I hurt you worse.

1029
01:24:25.320 --> 01:24:26.810
I respect your creed.

1030
01:24:27.800 --> 01:24:29.564
Mm, good.

1031
01:24:30.760 --> 01:24:32.140
[CRACKLES]

1032
01:24:32.240 --> 01:24:34.004
- [ELECTRICITY CRACKLING]
- [GRUNTS]

1033
01:24:37.200 --> 01:24:39.089
AKHMADOV: Over there.

1034
01:24:59.160 --> 01:25:00.860
Sir, I have something.

1035
01:25:00.960 --> 01:25:03.580
Akhmadov. Russian FSB operative.

1036
01:25:03.680 --> 01:25:06.968
What's he doing arriving
on a fishing boat in Dagenham?

1037
01:25:07.120 --> 01:25:08.740
QUAKER: The Russians aren't stupid enough

1038
01:25:08.840 --> 01:25:10.340
to try making a move
from their own embassy.

1039
01:25:10.440 --> 01:25:14.220
They're bringing in a grab team
to pick up the Dutchman.

1040
01:25:14.320 --> 01:25:15.924
Get me in the air now!

1041
01:25:31.480 --> 01:25:35.460
He'll be on the A11,
headed right toward us.

1042
01:25:35.560 --> 01:25:38.325
